    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0422" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R294/828</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The German Chargé (Leitner) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">St. D.A. 14</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-27">September 27, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith to Your Excellency two letters of this date,<anchor n="65"
                        xml:id="d227-f1"/> addressed to the Secretary <pb facs="0423" n="333"
                        xml:id="pg333"/> of the Treasury of the United States with the request to
                    forward them to the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>In these letters, I have, by direction of my Government, explained to the
                    Treasury Department of the United States in accordance with Sections 5 and 8 of
                    the German-American Debt Agreement of June 23, 1930 that Germany will postpone
                    the payments due on September 30, 1932 under Sections 1<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a</hi> and 1<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi> of the aforesaid Agreement for
                    the claims allowed by the German-American Mixed Commission and for the amounts
                    owing for payment of arrears in costs of the American Army of Occupation.</p>
                <p>With the renewed assurance [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Leitner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
